## 🧠 The complete picture

This is the most important sequence to understand:

```text
PC1 wants to ping PC3
        ↓
PC1 knows PC3's IP
        ↓
PC1 doesn't know PC3's MAC
        ↓
ARP Request
(Broadcast)
        ↓
Switch floods it
        ↓
PC3 receives it
        ↓
ARP Reply
(Unicast)
        ↓
PC1 learns PC3's MAC
        ↓
PC1 sends ICMP Echo Request
(Unicast)
        ↓
PC3 sends ICMP Echo Reply
(Unicast)
```

If you understand this sequence, you've connected **ARP + Ethernet + MAC learning + switching + ICMP + ping** into one practical process. 
